    "title": "Restaurant roundup: Centro's fishing-inspired bar, new brewery for Longfellow - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Audrey Kennedy ,\n18 hours ago\nAfter purchasing the former Chicago Taste Authority property last month, Centro Restaurant Group announced it will open Bill's Bait Shop, a bar and restaurant inspired by northern Minnesota fishing culture.\nExpect the atmosphere of your neighborhood dive bar and a \"comforting, approachable\" menu, per Minneapolis/St. Paul Business Journal . It will tentatively open in June. 🍻 Dangerous Man Brewing will revive its Northeast Minneapolis taproom, this time in the soon-to-be-vacated HeadFlyer Brewing space, the Minnesota Star Tribune reports .\nLook for an end-of-spring opening. 🍝 Risata Cucina , a modern Italian-American restaurant from industry veterans, is now open in downtown Robbinsdale.\nExpect a wide variety of pastas — all under $25 — and one of the largest amaro collections in the state, per Mpls.St.Paul Magazine . 🛒 David Fhima 's new grocery store venture The Global Table is set to open inside the new Coborn's in Plymouth on March 12, per a release.\n🚴 A new brewery — and then some — is in the works on the corner of 45th and Minnehaha. Mixed Culture Brewing, run by industry veterans, will operate as a coffee shop in the morning before transitioning to a taproom with live music and a large beer garden, Longfellow Whatever reports .\nOwners also plan to host a bike shop in the space, which was formerly home to One on One Bike Shop. Expect an opening sometime this year. 🍭 Oppa Sweets, the whimsical cotton candy stand we wrote about last week , is \"temporarily\" closing its Mall of America outpost at the end of a month, per its social media . Its Maplewood Mall location will remain open.\n👋 Downtown Wayzata restaurant ninetwentyfive is becoming Belle & Grey, an all-day spot under the same ownership, per its social media . Expect a spring debut.\n4",
    "summary": "🍝 Risata Cucina , a modern Italian-American restaurant from industry veterans, is now open in downtown Robbinsdale. 🛒 David Fhima 's new grocery store venture The Global Table is set to open inside the new Coborn's in Plymouth on March 12, per a release. Mixed Culture Brewing, run by industry veterans, will operate as a coffee shop in the morning before transitioning to a taproom with live music and a large beer garden, Longfellow Whatever reports .",
